{"id": "EUVD-2026-71615", "enisaUuid": "15913873-3234-33da-9052-a76aa924f2b6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: reject an unclaimed class value in security_get_classes()\n\nsecurity_get_classes() sizes an array by p_classes.nprim and fills it at\nvalue - 1, so a class value the policy never defines leaves a NULL.\nsel_make_classes() passes every entry to sel_make_dir(), reaching the same\nd_alloc_name() dereference as the permission array. The class symbol table\nis allowed to be sparse (policydb_class_isvalid() exists to absorb that),\nbut this getter builds its own array straight from the hash table and has\nno such predicate.\n\nFail the lookup when a value went unclaimed instead of handing out the\nNULL. Conforming policies define every class they declare and are\nunaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T17:19:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T11:58:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2e7f7035d6f407119ba5467f7218cc4370844fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f38a71868888285efc9c0ab5b032e23919c5a0a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3480c081c23d559fd9a6921b76955664f2e95153", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0285bb152211c00900136b66d4b420c14a59094", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/099869e9343a5f8c22b58497f074b34f63cbf856", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/841aea4d5a25e16273d04cd07a74142b4687e03b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8a10899ea3c84b80de72ca8ee9039e9a5156c9a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22b05fec62c0fe9864cfceb52f7d0f3a34d9b1dd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80912", "GHSA-5v22-vqg5-vrr8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "027b0e44-5867-3aaf-900f-92a27c0ea94c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55fcf09b3fe4325c9395ebbb0322a547a157ebc7 <d8a10899ea3c84b80de72ca8ee9039e9a5156c9a"}, {"id": "0c7106a4-5c29-3342-987f-4327c1a919ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "26f40a99-3dd5-3c29-bea6-9566f656fa3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55fcf09b3fe4325c9395ebbb0322a547a157ebc7 <e0285bb152211c00900136b66d4b420c14a59094"}, {"id": "27194c34-53f7-3113-96bd-485bf4bdc5b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "2f0a63d8-1a8f-30a3-ab6e-60c33e5b5fcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6484ffd2-0275-35e0-8cae-2efaa808ca61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.23"}, {"id": "67cfcb80-a5a8-39f8-b458-024a4b38433a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "686fb761-dbb6-3e7c-84ec-db4cca670304", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "745c06bc-1614-3749-8f00-b0e23b11d865", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55fcf09b3fe4325c9395ebbb0322a547a157ebc7 <3480c081c23d559fd9a6921b76955664f2e95153"}, {"id": "83ad62bc-8a19-35f4-b5bb-0331ef7ffbd9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.153"}, {"id": "90eb6ab0-5726-3b13-8e23-476de27f64cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.46"}, {"id": "97423460-71e7-3681-a576-876216ef33cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55fcf09b3fe4325c9395ebbb0322a547a157ebc7 <d2e7f7035d6f407119ba5467f7218cc4370844fc"}, {"id": "a6dcd11b-3281-31f1-86e9-173656cbf2e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.105"}, {"id": "aa7af126-b618-3467-8ba3-557dd80d0b4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55fcf09b3fe4325c9395ebbb0322a547a157ebc7 <22b05fec62c0fe9864c